                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Operation KREEP is a game about a team of astronauts removing a dangerous and rapidly growing alien infestation from a space station. You can have up to four human/AI players using the same keyboard - but that may be tricky if you have four human players. The players ''win'' if they successfully wipe out the infestation. As the game opens though, the players are subjected to a message from a corporation promising money if they leave the infestation alive, and kill off their teammates. This creates a game-theory conundrum in which players can either work together to win, or go rogue for a big win at the detriment to the other players. Spoiler: noone ever wins though: cooperative teams go to prison for damaging the station. Rogue players are left to drift through space.\n\nGameplay-wise, it's a bit like bomberman with guns instead of bombs. Move around with your arrow-key equivalent, shoot the kreep (or your teammates) by pressing the shoot button.\n\nThe base game is a little dull to be honest - the kreep growth is balanced so well that a single player going rogue will almost inevitably result in Kreep overtaking the station, but a cooperative team will almost always overwhelm the kreep. This is easily remedied however, because the game has a number of ''mutators'' - alternate game settings. I recommend rockets and slow rockets - sure this makes it easier to kill the kreep, but that leaves more room for backstabbing shenanigans.\n\nIf you're going to spend a few dollars on a desktop game, you could do worse.",
